      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers arrived on horseback, then moved on to trains, trolleys, automobiles, and buses as transportation evolved.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://plainfieldlibrary.info/OnlineExhibits/ONTHEMOVE/one_1.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town was designed for walking; most residents lived within a short stroll of their workplaces.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://plainfieldlibrary.info/OnlineExhibits/ONTHEMOVE/one_1.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rich city folk rented carriages to vacation in Plainfield, bringing craftsmen who built elegant summer homes and fine clothing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://plainfieldlibrary.info/OnlineExhibits/ONTHEMOVE/one_1.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the early 19th century, people flocked to Plainfield seeking open space, opportunity, and freedom of religion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
